{"severity":"warning","file":"errors/vault_check_then_act_1.march","start_line":7,"start_col":4,"end_line":7,"end_col":32,"message":"This writes `page` in `hits` based on a value read from it earlier, and another writer can change it in between.","code":"vault_check_then_act","fix":null,"labels":[{"file":"errors/vault_check_then_act_1.march","start_line":6,"start_col":12,"end_line":6,"end_col":39,"message":"`page` read here"}],"notes":["`Vault.get_or` and `Vault.set` each take the table's lock, but nothing holds it between them. If another task or actor writes `page` in that window, this write replaces its value and that update is lost.","For a counter, `Vault.incr(table, key, delta)` adds and returns the new value under one lock, so concurrent increments are never lost.","If only one task ever writes this table, mark the function `@[no_warn_race]`."],"category":"CONCURRENCY"}
